# Bench configuration for the manual tests. Copy to tests/.env and edit.
#
#   cd tests
#   uv run --env-file .env pytest manual/gpio_loopback/gpio_loopback.py -v -s
#
# Everything here has a default that works on the author's bench, so an unset
# variable is not an error - it just means "the author's board". .env itself is
# gitignored; this example file is the documentation.

# --- serial port --------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed where a port has to be named: the pytest sketch tests take --port,
# and the manual tools discover the probe by USB VID:PID + serial so they need
# nothing here. Uncomment and set if your setup needs it.
#
# If your host publishes stable per-device symlinks (a udev rule, or boards
# arriving over USBIP where the number is not fixed), point at one of those
# instead of the raw device - the number moves, the name does not.
# CH32_PORT=/dev/ttyACM0

# --- naming the probes --------------------------------------------------------
# manual/probe_switch reads every CH32_PROBE_<NAME> and lets you say the name
# instead of the serial:
#
#   CH32_PROBE_V103=434A124C5596
#   CH32_PROBE_X035=FC928F068181
#
#   uv run --env-file tests/.env tests/manual/probe_switch/probe_switch.py V103
#
# The names are yours; only the CH32_PROBE_ prefix is fixed. Use the USB serial
# and not the COM number or the USB/IP bus id: the serial is burned into the
# probe, a COM number follows the physical port it is plugged into, and a bus id
# is renumbered whenever anything is replugged.
#
# Only useful where probes arrive over USB/IP (usbipd-win on a WSL host).
# Elsewhere probe_switch has nothing to switch and says so.

# --- manual/chip_info, manual/smoke, manual/uart_scan -------------------------
# These take no pytest options: pytest-embedded already owns --port and --target,
# and a second meaning for either would be worse than a variable. Every one of
# them has a working default, so an unset variable is not an error.
#
# CH32_PROBE          WCH-Link USB serial, or any prefix. Needed only when more
#                     than one probe is attached.
# CH32_BOARD          Assert which board this is, e.g. CH32X035. Normally
#                     unnecessary - probe-rs reads the part number and
#                     boards.txt maps it back, so the image cannot be built for
#                     a board other than the one it is flashed to. Needed for
#                     the [compile only] series, which have no probe-rs target.
# CH32_FORCE=1        Flash even when the attached chip is a different series.
# CH32_PNUM           Part number menu entry (default ANY, which is what the
#                     profiles and most users build). 'detect' uses the exact
#                     part probe-rs reports.
# CH32_SKETCH         Which of tests/sketches/basic to run, or 'all' - one
#                     pytest case per sketch. Default: serial_println.
# CH32_SERIAL_INDEX   Override which USART Serial is, when this board wires a
#                     different one than the variant chose. The uart_scan test
#                     finds it; bench.json is where it belongs permanently.
# CH32_BAUD           Default 115200.
# CH32_SECONDS        How long to listen after flashing. Default 4 (12 for
#                     uart_scan, which drives every route in turn).
# CH32_BUILD_PROPERTY Extra --build-property for the compile, space separated.
#                     For trying something the board definition does not offer,
#                     e.g. CH32_BUILD_PROPERTY=build.f_cpu=24000000L to run the
#                     part off a divided clock.

# --- manual/reg_probe ---------------------------------------------------------
# Which tool reads the registers through the probe. probe-rs (default) is in
# .tools; ch32rv reads about five times faster and is the tool the platform is
# moving to. Either way the WCH-LinkE rewrites the target's clock on every
# attach - the sketch heals that itself (manual/README.ja.md, reg_probe).
# CH32_READER=ch32rv
# CH32_CH32RV=/path/to/ch32rv        # when ch32rv is not on PATH

# --- manual/gpio_loopback -----------------------------------------------------
# The two pads the jumper connects. Different ports, nothing else driving them,
# and never the SWD pads (PA13/PA14, or PC18/PC19 on X033/X035).
#   CH32X035 (LQFP48): PA0 / PB0
#   CH32V003 (TSSOP20): PA1 / PC0
# A plain pin number also works if the pad name is not one this parser knows.
CH32_LOOPBACK_OUT=PA0
CH32_LOOPBACK_IN=PB0
